      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ يَقُولُ: «لاَ بَأْسَ بِأَنْ يُصَلِّيَ اَلرَّجُلُ رَكْعَتَيْنِ مِنَ اَلْوَتْرِ ثُمَّ يَنْصَرِفَ فَيَقْضِيَ حَاجَتَهُ ثُمَّ يَرْجِعَ فَيُصَلِّيَ رَكْعَةً."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1417 - It is narrated from Abu Walad Hafs bin Salim Al-Hannat that He said:\n\"I heard Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) say,\n'There is no harm if a person prays two units (rak‘ahs) of Witr prayer, then turns away to fulfil a need, and then returns to pray one unit (rak‘ah).'\"."
        ]
      }
